1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,011
Photosynthesis. Inputs, process and outputs, in one visual flow.

2
00:00:06,730 --> 00:00:09,285
A person eats a plate of food. That is

3
00:00:09,285 --> 00:00:12,417
how an animal gets its food: from outside. Now

4
00:00:12,417 --> 00:00:15,166
try the same with a plant. Nobody puts a

5
00:00:15,166 --> 00:00:18,250
plate of food in front of it. And yet

6
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:21,900
the plant keeps growing. New leaves open, and fruits

7
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:24,865
form. So where does a plant's food come from?

8
00:00:24,865 --> 00:00:27,397
The answer begins in one green leaf. The leaf

9
00:00:27,397 --> 00:00:28,601
can help make it.

10
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:33,220
What does photosynthesis need? Four things. Water comes from

11
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:35,670
the soil, and the roots carry it up to

12
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:38,741
the leaf. Carbon dioxide comes from the air around

13
00:00:38,741 --> 00:00:43,150
the leaf. Light energy comes from the Sun. And

14
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:47,537
chlorophyll, the green pigment, is already inside the green

15
00:00:47,537 --> 00:00:51,388
parts of the plant. Water, carbon dioxide, light and

16
00:00:51,388 --> 00:00:53,201
chlorophyll: these are the four requirements.

17
00:00:53,850 --> 00:00:55,450
But the four do not play the same role.

18
00:00:55,450 --> 00:00:58,314
Carbon dioxide and water are the chemical materials. They

19
00:00:58,314 --> 00:01:02,050
are the matter that gets used. Light is the

20
00:01:02,050 --> 00:01:05,320
energy source. It supplies energy, but it does not

21
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:11,730
become part of the food. Chlorophyll is the light-capturing

22
00:01:11,730 --> 00:01:14,250
pigment. It helps to catch the light, and it

23
00:01:14,250 --> 00:01:16,430
is not used up like water. Materials, energy and

24
00:01:16,430 --> 00:01:20,376
pigment work together in photosynthesis. So needed for the

25
00:01:20,376 --> 00:01:22,361
process does not mean consumed in the same way.

26
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,331
Where does all this happen? Zoom into a leaf.

27
00:01:26,331 --> 00:01:28,535
Inside it are cells, and each green cell holds

28
00:01:28,535 --> 00:01:31,240
many small green bodies. One of them is a

29
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:35,920
chloroplast. The chloroplast is the site of photosynthesis. Carbon

30
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:39,460
dioxide, water and light all meet here. We will

31
00:01:39,460 --> 00:01:41,911
open the chloroplast in the next video.

32
00:01:42,550 --> 00:01:47,710
Now, what does the chloroplast make? Carbon dioxide enters

33
00:01:47,710 --> 00:01:51,358
from the air. Water arrives from the soil. Light

34
00:01:51,358 --> 00:01:56,870
energy switches the chloroplast on. Inside, it is not

35
00:01:56,870 --> 00:02:01,378
one step. A series of reactions takes place, with

36
00:02:01,378 --> 00:02:08,050
several intermediate compounds. The main product is glucose, a

37
00:02:08,050 --> 00:02:16,394
carbohydrate. The light energy is now stored in it

38
00:02:16,394 --> 00:02:19,072
as chemical energy.

39
00:02:19,797 --> 00:02:23,741
Photosynthesis also gives out a gas. Oxygen forms inside

40
00:02:23,741 --> 00:02:27,077
the chloroplast. It leaves the cell, and then the

41
00:02:27,077 --> 00:02:30,557
leaf, and goes out into the air. So, in:

42
00:02:30,557 --> 00:02:35,222
carbon dioxide and water, with light. Out: glucose and

43
00:02:35,222 --> 00:02:39,848
oxygen. The purpose is food. Oxygen is an important

44
00:02:39,848 --> 00:02:42,588
product that is released along the way.

45
00:02:43,173 --> 00:02:46,693
Now let us read the equation as a story.

46
00:02:46,693 --> 00:02:49,600
In words: carbon dioxide plus water, with light and

47
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:54,533
chlorophyll, gives glucose, water and oxygen. Carbon dioxide is

48
00:02:54,533 --> 00:02:56,765
C O two. Water is H two O, and

49
00:02:56,765 --> 00:02:59,717
glucose is C six H twelve O six. Now

50
00:02:59,717 --> 00:03:04,587
the numbers. The textbook equation is: six C O

51
00:03:04,587 --> 00:03:07,833
two plus twelve H two O, in light and

52
00:03:07,833 --> 00:03:10,593
chlorophyll, gives C six H twelve O six, plus

53
00:03:10,593 --> 00:03:13,982
six H two O, plus six O two. Notice

54
00:03:13,982 --> 00:03:16,923
that water appears on both sides, twelve going in

55
00:03:16,923 --> 00:03:21,166
and six coming out. So overall, six water molecules

56
00:03:21,166 --> 00:03:24,993
are used, and the net equation is six C

57
00:03:24,993 --> 00:03:27,233
O two plus six H two O gives C

58
00:03:27,233 --> 00:03:30,104
six H twelve O six plus six O two.

59
00:03:30,670 --> 00:03:34,561
Glucose is only the beginning of plant material. Many

60
00:03:34,561 --> 00:03:39,250
glucose units can join into larger carbohydrates. Glucose can

61
00:03:39,250 --> 00:03:42,427
be used to form starch, which the plant stores,

62
00:03:42,427 --> 00:03:45,370
and cellulose, which builds the cell wall. Each arrow

63
00:03:45,370 --> 00:03:48,895
says can be used to form, because each takes

64
00:03:48,895 --> 00:03:52,981
more steps. So photosynthesis provides the starting food material.

65
00:03:53,497 --> 00:03:57,825
Your turn. Complete the photosynthesis map. A: which gas

66
00:03:57,825 --> 00:04:00,577
enters the leaf from the air? B: what is

67
00:04:00,577 --> 00:04:03,753
carried up from the roots? C: which is the

68
00:04:03,753 --> 00:04:06,985
energy source? D: which food is made inside the

69
00:04:06,985 --> 00:04:10,087
plant? E: which gas is released into the air?

70
00:04:10,087 --> 00:04:14,797
And two quick checks: which supplies energy, carbon dioxide

71
00:04:14,797 --> 00:04:19,275
or sunlight? And where does photosynthesis happen? Take your

72
00:04:19,275 --> 00:04:21,288
time, and pause the video if you need to.

73
00:04:32,653 --> 00:04:36,633
Let us check. A: carbon dioxide. B: water. C:

74
00:04:36,633 --> 00:04:40,773
light energy from the Sun. D: glucose. E: oxygen.

75
00:04:40,773 --> 00:04:47,250
Sunlight supplies the energy, not carbon dioxide, and photosynthesis

76
00:04:47,250 --> 00:04:48,964
happens in the chloroplast.

77
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:52,100
Here is the whole story. Water rises from the

78
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:55,340
soil. Carbon dioxide enters the leaf. Sunlight strikes the

79
00:04:55,340 --> 00:05:00,900
leaf. Chlorophyll in the chloroplast captures the light. Photosynthesis

80
00:05:00,900 --> 00:05:04,749
happens inside. Glucose stays in the plant, and oxygen

81
00:05:04,749 --> 00:05:07,864
goes out into the air. Simple materials plus light

82
00:05:07,864 --> 00:05:14,305
energy become energy-rich food. Input, transform, output. But how

83
00:05:14,305 --> 00:05:16,525
does one chloroplast capture light and build food? Next

84
00:05:16,525 --> 00:05:21,616
time: grana, stroma and the pigments. Thank you for

85
00:05:21,616 --> 00:05:23,871
watching, and see you in the next lesson.
